# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/engine-reuse four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window's combined branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-engine-reuse-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the combined branch (the W2 + Lever N + prefix route with engine reuse merged
# in); substitute it in every template with one command (sed -i 's/tp4-engine-reuse-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every
# template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# B0 (no card opened): build the window image from the pushed combined commit. The profile named is the production default; nothing is baked as the image default (no C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE).
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that already exists. What the image carries that is new: serving_parked_engines (docker/qwen-c2-overlay.txt) and the changed
# verifier_engine_tp, serving_request_factory, serving_runtime, serving_lifecycle, serving_worker_hook, serving_fast_request, serving_buffer_pool, dflash_packed_proposal_coordinator,
# serving_prefill_admission, levern_policy, memory_ledger, serving_fast_policy, serving_c2_contract and qwen_c2_profiles.json; every engine-reuse profile is gate only, never baked.
# READ: the build log's provenance report with no problem line, the closure checks pass, the image id printed. Never run it during a timing job. Stop rule: a build or provenance failure stops the window.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-engine-reuse-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
